            <ArticleTitle>Musculoskeletal chest wall pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-23, 27</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Costosternal syndrome is a pretender of serious illness and mimes as a variety of conditions; essentially the diagnosis is clinical, identified by physical examination and intuition. Reassurance is the most common treatment to this often self-limiting condition that is a common cause of chest wall pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
